description:
Out here towards the end of the jetty, you feel quite isolated. Gone;
are the sounds of the beach, the birds, the waves on the shoreline.;
All you hear are the rhythmic crash of waves against the jetty which;
turns northwest from here toward the other jetty. Continuing that;
direction would be unwise, the waves are just too violent.

This small building appears to be both the living quarters and storage area
for the keep's groundkeeper.  Some wicked looking lawn tools hang on one wall,
and a small bed and table stand opposite them.
